---
/**
 * The O*NET attribution block, in the exact form USDOL/ETA requires.
 *
 * Their terms are specific: the O*NET-in-it mark, linked to
 * services.onetcenter.org, plus the sentence naming the U.S. Department of
 * Labor, Employment and Training Administration and the trademark notice.
 * Wording and link target are not ours to improve on, so this component exists
 * to keep one exact copy rather than a paraphrase per page.
 *
 * Use it on every page that renders O*NET data — the skills graph, occupation
 * pages, and anywhere skills or wage structure comes from O*NET — and on
 * /sources/ where the feed is listed. Not on pages that merely link to one of
 * those, because attribution belongs where the data is shown.
 *
 * The image is served from onetcenter.org rather than self-hosted: it is their
 * mark, and pulling a local copy would leave us serving a stale version of
 * somebody else's trademark. It is the one deliberate exception to the
 * self-hosted-assets rule, so it carries width, height, and loading="lazy" to
 * keep it off the critical path.
 */
---
<p class="onet">
  <a
    href="https://services.onetcenter.org/"
    title="This site incorporates information from O*NET Web Services. Click to learn more."
    rel="noopener"
  >
    <img
      src="https://www.onetcenter.org/image/link/onet-in-it.svg"
      width="130"
      height="60"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="O*NET in-it"
    />
  </a>
</p>
<p class="onet-note">
  This site incorporates information from
  <a href="https://services.onetcenter.org/" rel="noopener">O*NET Web Services</a>
  by the U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training Administration
  (USDOL/ETA). O*NET&reg; is a trademark of USDOL/ETA.
</p>

<style>
  .onet { text-align: center; margin: 1.6em 0 .4em; }
  .onet img { border: none; width: 130px; height: 60px; }
  .onet-note { font-size: .87rem; color: #6b6b78; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 720px; }
</style>
